#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""fleet-skill-apply — apply a retro proposal diff (generic skill or project lessons), with a ledger and exact revert.

  fleet-skill-apply DIFF --run RUN --reason "why"            check, back up, apply, append a ledger line
  fleet-skill-apply --revert ID [--scope S] [--reason "why"]  restore the exact bytes recorded before ledger entry ID
  options: --relation new|refines:<id>|supersedes:<id> (stored in the ledger entry; the rules index rebuilds its
           superseded history from it), --check (only check), --scope generic|project:<name> (assert/choose the ledger; default: from the diff
           paths), --allow-active (apply to always-loaded files while a fleet lead runs), --force (revert after drift)
           --op add|edit|merge|archive|legacy  what the diff is (fleet-retro prints it in the suggested command)
           --drops '<JSON list>'  backtick literals the change removes on purpose (merge-guard; stored in the ledger)
           --archive-kind redundancy|supersession|error --evidence TEXT  required with --op archive
           --decision ID --cand-fp FP  judge decision id / candidate fingerprint, stored in the ledger entry (optional)
           --txn ID  transaction id linking entries (promotion: the generic apply and the project archives), stored
           --probation  generic rule applied in probation (PLAN F4): entry gets probation: true, the rules it adds get
                        index status "probation"; generic scope and ONE file only. fleet_probation decides later
                        (auto-revert / active). --failure-probe ID (fail-<16 hex>) names the failure it targets.
           --auto-revert-of ID  with --revert ID only, used by fleet_probation.auto_revert: the revert entry gets
                        auto_revert: true + auto_revert_of (target must be in probation). A --reason starting with
                        "auto-revert " is refused without it (a manual revert never passes as an auto-revert).

Probation slots (F3.1 rule 5, checked before --check returns and again under the ledger lock): an always-loaded file
(policy always_loaded) holds at most policy probation.max_per_always_loaded_file rules in probation; while one is in
probation every other change to that file is refused (a later change would make its revert drift). --revert is never
blocked.

Merge-guard (code, 0 tokens, same fleet_skill_lib.merge_guard as fleet-retro validate): unless --op archive or the manual
human flag --op legacy (fleet-retro never prints it; recorded as declared_op), every file of the diff is checked alone by
fleet_skill_lib.guard_change, per rule block: every removed old block must have a replacement block (its most similar
added block in the same changed region) that is >= policy merge_guard.min_ratio x the old block and keeps every
backtick literal of it unless it is in --drops; an old block with no replacement is a deletion (use --op archive). The
refusal names the missing literal. The proposal metadata <diff>.ops.json written by fleet-retro (or --ops PATH) is used
ONLY with --op merge, ONLY for its merge ops, and only to relax one case: an old block that is a source of a merge whose
sources and result the diff shows may have the merged block as its replacement (e.g. a merged block equal to one
source). The merges handed to the guard are recorded in the ledger entry (guard_merges: file + sha256 of the sources
and result; ops_sha256: sha256 of the ops file). Everything else is guarded on the diff alone. A --cand-fp is exempt
from the secret check only when it is exactly 64 lowercase hex chars (a sha256 cand_fp). --reason / --evidence / --decision / --cand-fp / every --drops entry holding a
secret-like string are refused.
Archive (--op archive): the diff must delete exactly one contiguous block of whole lines of one file; the exact bytes go to
skill/archive/<stamp>-<slug>.md (project scope: ORQ_ROOT/<project>/lessons-archive/) with a header (reason, evidence, ledger
id, source runs, file, anchor, offset) and the ledger line is op=archive. Nothing is deleted. `--revert ID` of an archive
entry puts the exact bytes back at the original offset (needs the file as the archive left it, or --force: then it is
placed by context), moves the archive file to <archive dir>/restored/ and the index status goes archived -> active.
Crash-safe retry: a file that already holds its exact pre-archive bytes is not touched again (no second insertion);
the revert only finishes the bookkeeping (archive move, ledger entry with placement already-restored, index).

Scopes (picked from the diff's paths; one scope per diff):
  generic  skill/... and .claude/agents/... (relative to the fleet root), learnings.md (relative to the Orquestra
           root) → FLEET_ROOT/skill/ledger.jsonl, backups FLEET_ROOT/skill/ledger-backups/<id>/
  project  <project>/LESSONS.md (relative to the Orquestra root) → ORQ_ROOT/<project>/lessons-ledger.jsonl,
           backups ORQ_ROOT/<project>/lessons-backups/<id>/
Ledger line: {id, ts, op, scope, base, run, files:[{path, sha256_before, sha256_after}], reason, diff_path, relation?,
relation_hash?}. relation_hash = full sha256 of the rule a refines/supersedes relation names, resolved against the
rules the diff removes or changes (refused when the id matches none or several of them); only that rule becomes
superseded in the rules index.
After an apply or a revert the scope's part of skill/rules-index.json is rebuilt from the files + ledger (best effort:
a failure is reported as "index_error", never undoes the change); a revert of a supersedes entry releases the hash.
Refused: renames/copies/mode changes/binary/deletions, headerless git sections, bookkeeping paths (ledger, lock,
backups, proposals, archive), symlinked targets. The diff is snapshotted once to a private temp file and every step
(validation, check, apply, backup copy) uses that snapshot, under the ledger lock.
Exit: 0 ok, 1 refused/not clean, 2 usage."""
import argparse, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, tempfile, time
sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import fleet_skill_lib as L
import fleet_rules_index as R
import fleet_probation as P

ALWAYS_LOADED = ("skill/fleet-sdd/SKILL.md", ".claude/agents/team-lead.md")


class Refuse(Exception):
    def __init__(self, obj, code=1):
        self.obj, self.code = obj, code


def refresh_index(obj, scope, archived=None):
    """Rebuild the rules index for this scope after a change (best effort; adds index_error on failure).
    archived: kwargs of fleet_rules_index.mark_archived (after an archive: the removed rules get status archived)."""
    try:
        R.rebuild_index([scope.label()])
        if archived:
            R.mark_archived(scope.label(), **archived)
    except Exception as e:   # the change itself is done and ledgered: never fail it because of the sidecar
        obj["index_error"] = f"{e.__class__.__name__}: {e}"[:300]
    return obj


def out(obj, code=0):
    print(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
    sys.exit(code)


def plan(snapshot, forced_scope):
    """Validate the snapshot → (scope, [rel]). Raises Refuse."""
    with open(snapshot, encoding="utf-8", errors="strict") as f:
        text = f.read()
    probs = L.patch_problems(text)
    if probs:
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "unsupported patch", "problems": probs[:10]})
    scope, rels = None, []
    for rel, is_new, is_del in L.diff_files(text):
        if is_del:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"diff deletes a file ({rel}); deletions are not allowed — archive instead"})
        sc, norm = L.scope_for_path(rel)
        if sc is None:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": norm})
        if scope is not None and (sc.key != scope.key or sc.base != scope.base):
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "diff mixes scopes/roots (split it: one diff per ledger)",
                          "files": rels + [norm]})
        scope = sc
        if norm in rels:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"file appears twice in the diff: {norm}"})
        rels.append(norm)
        link = L.symlink_in_path(scope.base, norm)
        if link:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"refusing symlinked path component {link}"})
    if forced_scope is not None and forced_scope.key != scope.key:
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"--scope {forced_scope.label()} does not match the diff ({scope.label()})"})
    paths, summary = L.git_patch_paths(snapshot, scope.base)
    if paths is None:
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "git cannot parse the diff", "detail": summary})
    created_ok = {f"create mode 100644 {r}" for r in rels}
    extra = [p for p in paths if p not in rels] + [s for s in summary if s not in created_ok]
    if extra or len(paths) != len(rels):
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "git would touch more than the validated files", "detail": extra[:10]})
    for d in (scope.ledger_dir, scope.backups):
        link = L.symlink_in_path(scope.anchor, scope.rel(d))
        if link:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"refusing symlinked bookkeeping path {link}"})
    return scope, rels


def decode(b):
    return "" if b is None else b.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")


def preview(snap, scope, rels):
    """{rel: (bytes before | None, bytes after | None)} of applying the snapshot to private copies of the touched files
    (the real tree is not modified) → (dict, None) | (None, git message)."""
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="fleet-skill-preview-")
    try:
        before = {}
        for rel in rels:
            src = os.path.join(scope.base, rel)
            before[rel] = None
            if os.path.isfile(src) and not os.path.islink(src):
                with open(src, "rb") as f:
                    before[rel] = f.read()
                dst = os.path.join(tmp, rel)
                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                with open(dst, "wb") as f:
                    f.write(before[rel])
        ok, msg = L.git_apply(snap, tmp, check_only=False)
        if not ok:
            return None, msg
        out = {}
        for rel in rels:
            p = os.path.join(tmp, rel)
            out[rel] = (before[rel], open(p, "rb").read() if os.path.isfile(p) else None)
        return out, None
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


def evaluate(snap, scope, rels, a):
    """Merge-guard / archive checks on the real current files → the archive plan (rel, offset, block, before, after)
    for --op archive, else None. Raises Refuse. Run before --check returns and again under the ledger lock."""
    changes, msg = preview(snap, scope, rels)
    if changes is None:
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "diff does not apply cleanly", "detail": (msg or "")[-1500:]})
    if a.op == "archive":
        if len(changes) != 1:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "an archive diff must touch exactly one file"})
        rel, (b, aft) = next(iter(changes.items()))
        if b is None or aft is None:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "an archive diff must remove a block from an existing file"})
        got = L.deleted_block(b, aft)
        if got is None or not got[1].strip():
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "an archive diff must delete exactly one contiguous block of whole "
                          "lines (and add nothing)"})
        return rel, got[0], got[1], b, aft
    if a.op == "legacy":   # manual human flag only (fleet-retro never prints it); recorded as declared_op
        return None
    ratio, drops = L.load_policy()["merge_guard"]["min_ratio"], a.drops or []
    a.guard_merges = []
    for rel, (b, aft) in sorted(changes.items()):   # one file at a time: never pooled across files
        merges = [o for o in (a.ops_meta or []) if isinstance(o, dict) and o.get("file") == rel and o.get("op") == "merge"
                  ] if a.op == "merge" else []   # the sidecar relaxation is honoured only for a declared merge
        ok, why = L.guard_change(decode(b), decode(aft), drops, ratio, merges)
        if not ok:
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": why, "guard": "merge-guard", "file": rel, "drops": drops})
        a.guard_merges += [merge_record(rel, o) for o in merges]
    return None


def _sha(text):
    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest() if isinstance(text, str) else None


def merge_record(rel, op):
    """Ledger record of one sidecar merge handed to the merge-guard: hashes only (the sidecar is not trusted text)."""
    srcs = op.get("sources") if isinstance(op.get("sources"), list) else []
    return {"file": rel, "sources_sha256": [_sha(s) for s in srcs], "new_sha256": _sha(op.get("new"))}


def load_ops_meta(path):
    """(the "ops" list of a <diff>.ops.json, sha256 of its bytes) — read once, like the diff snapshot; (None, None)
    when absent / not valid."""
    try:
        if not os.path.isfile(path) or os.path.islink(path) or os.path.getsize(path) > 2_000_000:
            return None, None
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            raw = f.read(2_000_001)
        obj = json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None, None
    ops = obj.get("ops") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None
    return (ops, hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()) if isinstance(ops, list) else (None, None)


def check_probation(a, scope, rels, led):
    """F3.1 rule 5 / PLAN F4 gate (code). Raises Refuse."""
    if a.probation and (scope.kind != "generic" or len(rels) != 1):
        raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": "--probation needs a generic diff touching exactly one file (one rule per "
                      "ledger entry)", "files": rels})
    if scope.kind != "generic":
        return
    pol = L.load_policy()
    for rel in rels:
        holders = P.probation_holders(rel, led)
        if rel not in pol["always_loaded"] or not holders:
            continue
        if not a.probation or not P.probation_slot_free(rel, policy=pol, ledger=led):
            raise Refuse({"ok": False, "error": f"{rel} has a rule in probation (ledger entry {', '.join(holders)}); at "
                          f"most {pol['probation']['max_per_always_loaded_file']} per always-loaded file and no other "
                          "change to it until the probation ends (active or auto-reverted)", "probation": holders})


def apply(a, forced_scope):
    if not os.path.isfile(a.diff):
        out({"ok": False, "error": f"diff not found: {a.diff}"}, 2)
    tmpd = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="fleet-skill-apply-")
    try:
        snap = os.path.join(tmpd, "change.diff")
        with open(a.diff, "rb") as src, open(snap, "wb") as dst:   # one read; every later step uses these bytes
            dst.write(src.read())
        a.ops_meta, a.ops_sha256 = load_ops_meta(a.ops or a.diff + ".ops.json")
        try:
            scope, rels = plan(snap, forced_scope)
        except Refuse as r:
            out(r.obj, r.code)
        rel_hash = None
        if a.relation:   # refines/supersedes name exactly one rule the diff removes or changes: store its full hash
            with open(snap, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
                rel_hash, why = R.resolve_relation_hash(a.relation, f.read())
            if why:
                out({"ok": False, "error": why}, 1)
        ok, msg = L.git_apply(snap, scope.base, check_only=True)
        if not ok:
            out({"ok": False, "error": "diff does not apply cleanly", "detail": msg[-1500:]}, 1)
        try:
            evaluate(snap, scope, rels, a)
            check_probation(a, scope, rels, L.read_ledger(scope))
        except Refuse as r:
            out(r.obj, r.code)
        with open(snap, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
            added_hashes = P.added_rule_hashes(f.read()) if a.probation else []
        if a.check:
            out({"ok": True, "check_only": True, "scope": scope.label(), "files": rels})
        hot = [r for r in rels if r in ALWAYS_LOADED and scope.base == L.fleet_root()]
        leads = L.active_leads()
        if leads and hot and not a.allow_active:
            out({"ok": False, "error": "a fleet lead is running and the diff touches an always-loaded file; retry when it "
                 "ends or pass --allow-active", "active": leads, "files": hot}, 1)
        with L.LedgerLock(scope):
            ok, msg = L.git_apply(snap, scope.base, check_only=True)   # re-check under the lock (files may have moved)
            if not ok:
                out({"ok": False, "error": "diff no longer applies cleanly", "detail": msg[-1500:]}, 1)
            try:
                arch = evaluate(snap, scope, rels, a)   # again under the lock: the files may have moved
                check_probation(a, scope, rels, L.read_ledger(scope))
            except Refuse as r:
                out(r.obj, r.code)
            lid = L.next_id(scope)
            bdir = L.ensure_dir(scope.anchor, scope.rel(os.path.join(scope.backups, lid)))
            arch_info = write_archive(a, scope, lid, arch) if arch else None
            entry_files = []
            for rel in rels:
                src = os.path.join(scope.base, rel)
                before = L.sha256_file(src)
                if before is not None:
                    with open(src, "rb") as f:
                        L.safe_write(bdir, os.path.join("before", rel), f.read())
                entry_files.append({"path": rel, "sha256_before": before})
            with open(snap, "rb") as f:
                L.safe_write(bdir, "change.diff", f.read())
            ok, msg = L.git_apply(snap, scope.base, check_only=False)
            if not ok:   # should not happen after the check; restore what we saved
                restore(scope, bdir, entry_files)
                out({"ok": False, "error": "git apply failed after a clean check; files restored", "detail": msg[-1500:]}, 1)
            for f in entry_files:
                f["sha256_after"] = L.sha256_file(os.path.join(scope.base, f["path"]))
            entry = {"id": lid, "ts": L.now_iso(), "op": "archive" if arch else "apply", "scope": scope.label(),
                     "base": scope.base, "run": a.run, "files": entry_files, "reason": a.reason,
                     "diff_path": os.path.abspath(a.diff), "diff_copy": os.path.join(bdir, "change.diff")}
            if arch_info:
                entry.update(archive_file=arch_info["rel"], archive_kind=a.archive_kind, evidence=a.evidence,
                             offset=arch_info["offset"], block_sha256=arch_info["sha"])
            if a.op:
                entry["declared_op"] = a.op
            if a.drops:
                entry["drops"] = a.drops
            if getattr(a, "guard_merges", None):   # the sidecar merges the merge-guard was given (--op merge only)
                entry["guard_merges"] = a.guard_merges
                entry["ops_sha256"] = a.ops_sha256
            if a.decision:
                entry["decision_id"] = a.decision
            if a.cand_fp:
                entry["cand_fp"] = a.cand_fp
            if a.relation:
                entry["relation"] = a.relation
            if rel_hash:
                entry["relation_hash"] = rel_hash
            if a.txn:
                entry["txn"] = a.txn
            if a.probation:
                entry["probation"] = True
            if a.failure_probe:
                entry["failure_probe"] = a.failure_probe
            L.append_ledger(entry, scope)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmpd, ignore_errors=True)
    res = refresh_index({"ok": True, "ledger": entry}, scope,
                        archived=dict(block_text=decode(arch[2]), file=arch[0], anchor=arch_info["anchor"], ledger_id=lid,
                                      archive_file=arch_info["rel"], source_runs=arch_info["runs"]) if arch_info else None)
    if a.probation:   # after the rebuild: the rules this entry adds go to status probation (fleet_probation.sync_index
        try:          # re-derives it from the ledger after a crash here)
            res["probation_rules"] = P.mark_probation(added_hashes, lid)
        except Exception as e:
            res["index_error"] = f"{e.__class__.__name__}: {e}"[:300]
    out(res)


def write_archive(a, scope, lid, arch):
    """Write skill/archive/<stamp>-<slug>.md (header + the exact block bytes) BEFORE the change is applied, so the text
    can never be lost. → {rel (relative to scope.anchor), offset, sha, anchor, runs}"""
    rel, offset, block, before, after = arch
    text = decode(block)
    pos = len(decode(before[:offset]))
    anchor = R.anchor_at(decode(before), pos)
    prev = decode(before[:offset]).splitlines()
    runs = set()
    try:
        added = R.ledger_history(scope.label())[0]
        for r in R.rules_of_text(text):
            runs |= {str(run) for _, run in added.get(r["hash"], []) if run}
    except Exception:   # provenance is best effort
        pass
    sha = hashlib.sha256(block).hexdigest()
    meta = {"archive_version": 1, "ledger_id": lid, "scope": scope.label(), "file": rel, "anchor": anchor, "offset": offset,
            "prev_line": prev[-1] if prev else "", "block_sha256": sha, "sha256_before": hashlib.sha256(before).hexdigest(),
            "sha256_after": hashlib.sha256(after).hexdigest(), "reason_kind": a.archive_kind, "evidence": a.evidence,
            "reason": a.reason, "run": a.run, "source_runs": sorted(runs), "archived_at": L.now_iso()}
    arel = scope.rel(os.path.join(L.archive_dir(scope), f"{time.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')}-{lid}-{L.archive_slug(text)}.md"))
    L.safe_write(scope.anchor, arel, L.archive_pack(meta, block))
    return {"rel": arel, "offset": offset, "sha": sha, "anchor": anchor, "runs": sorted(runs)}


def place_by_context(cur, meta, block):
    """Bytes of `cur` with `block` put back when the file is no longer as the archive left it: after the line that
    preceded it, else under its heading, else at the start (offset 0) or the end."""
    if meta.get("offset") == 0:
        return block + cur
    prev = (meta.get("prev_line") or "").encode("utf-8")
    if prev.strip():
        i = cur.find(prev + b"\n")
        if i >= 0:
            return cur[:i + len(prev) + 1] + block + cur[i + len(prev) + 1:]
    head = (meta.get("anchor") or "").strip()
    if head:
        pos = 0
        for line in cur.splitlines(keepends=True):
            pos += len(line)
            if re.match(r"#{1,6}\s", decode(line)) and re.sub(r"^#+\s*", "", decode(line)).strip() == head:
                return cur[:pos] + block + cur[pos:]
    return (cur if not cur or cur.endswith(b"\n") else cur + b"\n") + block


def revert_archive(a, scope, target, base):
    """Revert of an op=archive entry (ledger lock held by the caller): put the archived bytes back, move the archive
    file to <archive dir>/restored/ (never delete), append the revert entry."""
    f = target["files"][0]
    rel = f["path"]
    adir = scope.rel(L.archive_dir(scope))
    norm = L._norm(target["archive_file"])
    if not norm or os.path.dirname(norm) != adir or not norm.endswith(".md"):
        out({"ok": False, "error": f"archive file outside {adir}: {target['archive_file']}"}, 1)
    link = L.symlink_in_path(scope.anchor, norm)
    if link:
        out({"ok": False, "error": f"refusing symlinked path component {link}"}, 1)
    apath = os.path.join(scope.anchor, norm)
    dest_rel = os.path.join(adir, "restored", os.path.basename(norm))
    cur_path = os.path.join(base, rel)
    cur_sha = L.sha256_file(cur_path)
    placement = "exact"
    if not os.path.isfile(apath):
        if not (cur_sha == f["sha256_before"] and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(scope.anchor, dest_rel))):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"archive file missing: {norm}"}, 1)
        placement, new = "already-restored", None   # a crash after the file was restored: finish the bookkeeping
    else:
        with open(apath, "rb") as fh:
            meta, block = L.archive_unpack(fh.read())
        if hashlib.sha256(block).hexdigest() != target.get("block_sha256") or meta.get("block_sha256") != target.get("block_sha256"):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"archive file {norm} does not match the ledger (corrupt)"}, 1)
        cur = b""
        if cur_sha is not None:
            with open(cur_path, "rb") as fh:
                cur = fh.read()
        if cur_sha is not None and cur_sha == f["sha256_before"]:
            # the file already holds the exact post-revert bytes (a crash after the restore, before the archive move):
            # never insert again, only finish the bookkeeping (move the archive, ledger revert entry, index)
            placement, new = "already-restored", None
        elif cur_sha == f["sha256_after"]:
            off = target["offset"]
            new = cur[:off] + block + cur[off:]
        elif not a.force:
            out({"ok": False, "error": "file changed after this archive (a later apply or a manual edit); revert later "
                 "entries first or pass --force to put the block back by context", "files": [rel]}, 1)
        else:
            new, placement = place_by_context(cur, meta, block), "context"
        if new is not None:
            L.safe_write(base, rel, new)
    lid = L.next_id(scope)
    if os.path.isfile(apath):
        L.ensure_dir(scope.anchor, os.path.dirname(dest_rel))
        dest, n = os.path.join(scope.anchor, dest_rel), 2
        while os.path.lexists(dest):
            dest, n = os.path.join(scope.anchor, f"{dest_rel[:-3]}-{n}.md"), n + 1
        os.replace(apath, dest)
        dest_rel = os.path.relpath(dest, scope.anchor)
    entry = {"id": lid, "ts": L.now_iso(), "op": "revert", "reverts": str(target["id"]), "scope": scope.label(),
             "base": base, "run": target.get("run"),
             "files": [{"path": rel, "sha256_before": cur_sha, "sha256_after": L.sha256_file(cur_path)}],
             "reason": a.reason or f"revert {target['id']}", "diff_path": target.get("diff_path"),
             "restored_archive": dest_rel, "placement": placement}
    L.append_ledger(entry, scope)
    out(refresh_index({"ok": True, "ledger": entry}, scope))


def restore(scope, bdir, files, base=None):
    base = base or scope.base
    for f in files:
        dst = os.path.join(base, f["path"])
        if f["sha256_before"] is None:
            if os.path.lexists(dst):   # created by the change: keep a copy, never just delete it
                L.ensure_dir(bdir, os.path.dirname(os.path.join("reverted-created", f["path"])))
                shutil.move(dst, os.path.join(bdir, "reverted-created", f["path"]))
        else:
            with open(os.path.join(bdir, "before", f["path"]), "rb") as fh:
                L.safe_write(base, f["path"], fh.read())


def revert(a, scope):
    with L.LedgerLock(scope):   # read, validate, restore and append under one lock
        led = L.read_ledger(scope)
        target = next((e for e in led if str(e.get("id")) == str(a.revert)), None)
        if not target or target.get("op") not in ("apply", "archive"):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"no apply entry with id {a.revert} in {scope.ledger}"}, 1)
        if target.get("op") == "archive" and not target.get("archive_file"):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"entry {a.revert} is a file-level archive by fleet-skill-lint: move the file back "
                 f"from its archived_to path by hand"}, 1)
        if any(e.get("op") == "revert" and str(e.get("reverts")) == str(a.revert) for e in led):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"entry {a.revert} was already reverted"}, 1)
        if a.auto_revert_of is not None and not (target.get("op") == "apply" and target.get("probation") is True):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"--auto-revert-of: entry {a.revert} is not an apply entry in probation"}, 1)
        base = target.get("base") or scope.base
        if base not in (L.fleet_root(), L.orq_root()):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"ledger entry base {base} is not the fleet or Orquestra root"}, 1)
        for f in target["files"]:
            sc, norm = L.scope_for_path(f["path"])
            if sc is None or sc.key != scope.key or norm != f["path"]:
                out({"ok": False, "error": f"ledger path not in this scope: {f['path']}"}, 1)
            link = L.symlink_in_path(base, f["path"])
            if link:
                out({"ok": False, "error": f"refusing symlinked path component {link}"}, 1)
        if target.get("op") == "archive":
            return revert_archive(a, scope, target, base)
        drift = [f["path"] for f in target["files"] if L.sha256_file(os.path.join(base, f["path"])) != f["sha256_after"]]
        if drift and not a.force:
            out({"ok": False, "error": "files changed after this entry (a later apply or a manual edit); revert later "
                 "entries first or pass --force", "files": drift}, 1)
        bdir = os.path.join(scope.backups, str(target["id"]))
        for f in target["files"]:
            if f["sha256_before"] is not None:
                b = os.path.join(bdir, "before", f["path"])
                if os.path.islink(b) or L.sha256_file(b) != f["sha256_before"]:
                    out({"ok": False, "error": f"backup missing or corrupt for {f['path']}"}, 1)
        lid = L.next_id(scope)
        cur = [{"path": f["path"], "sha256_before": L.sha256_file(os.path.join(base, f["path"]))} for f in target["files"]]
        restore(scope, bdir, target["files"], base)
        for c in cur:
            c["sha256_after"] = L.sha256_file(os.path.join(base, c["path"]))
        entry = {"id": lid, "ts": L.now_iso(), "op": "revert", "reverts": str(target["id"]), "scope": scope.label(),
                 "base": base, "run": target.get("run"), "files": cur, "reason": a.reason or f"revert {target['id']}",
                 "diff_path": target.get("diff_path")}
        if a.auto_revert_of is not None:   # structural marker: fleet_probation recognizes its own reverts by it
            entry.update(auto_revert=True, auto_revert_of=str(target["id"]))
        L.append_ledger(entry, scope)
    out(refresh_index({"ok": True, "ledger": entry}, scope))


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="fleet-skill-apply")
    ap.add_argument("diff", nargs="?")
    ap.add_argument("--run")
    ap.add_argument("--reason")
    ap.add_argument("--revert", metavar="ID")
    ap.add_argument("--scope", help="generic | project:<name> (default: from the diff; required for a project revert)")
    ap.add_argument("--check", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--allow-active", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--force", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--relation", help="new | refines:<rule id> | supersedes:<rule id> (stored in the ledger entry)")
    ap.add_argument("--op", choices=["add", "edit", "merge", "archive", "legacy"],
                    help="what the diff is; archive needs --archive-kind and --evidence; legacy (manual human flag "
                         "only) skips the merge-guard")
    ap.add_argument("--drops", help="JSON list of backtick literals the change removes on purpose (merge-guard)")
    ap.add_argument("--archive-kind", choices=list(L.ARCHIVE_KINDS))
    ap.add_argument("--evidence", help="why the block is redundant / superseded / wrong (required with --op archive)")
    ap.add_argument("--decision", help="judge decision_id (stored in the ledger entry)")
    ap.add_argument("--cand-fp", help="candidate fingerprint (stored in the ledger entry)")
    ap.add_argument("--txn", help="transaction id linking ledger entries (promotion), stored in the entry")
    ap.add_argument("--probation", action="store_true", help="apply a generic rule in probation (PLAN F4)")
    ap.add_argument("--failure-probe", help="failure probe id (fail-<16 hex>) the rule targets (probation recurrence)")
    ap.add_argument("--auto-revert-of", metavar="ID", help="with --revert ID only (fleet_probation.auto_revert's "
                    "argv): marks the revert entry auto_revert: true; the target must be a probation entry")
    ap.add_argument("--ops", help="proposal metadata for the merge-guard (default: DIFF.ops.json when it exists)")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.drops is not None:
        try:
            a.drops = json.loads(a.drops)
        except ValueError:
            a.drops = None
        if not isinstance(a.drops, list) or any(not isinstance(d, str) or not d.strip() for d in a.drops):
            ap.error("--drops must be a JSON list of non-empty strings")
    fp_digest = bool(a.cand_fp and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}", a.cand_fp))   # exactly a sha256 cand_fp: not a secret
    for flag, val in (("--reason", a.reason), ("--evidence", a.evidence), ("--decision", a.decision),
                      ("--cand-fp", None if fp_digest else a.cand_fp)) + tuple(("--drops", d) for d in (a.drops or [])):
        if L.has_secret(val):
            out({"ok": False, "error": f"{flag} contains a secret-like string: refused (it would persist in the ledger"
                 " / archive)"}, 1)
    if a.auto_revert_of is not None and (not a.revert or str(a.auto_revert_of) != str(a.revert)):
        ap.error("--auto-revert-of ID needs --revert with the same ID")
    if (a.reason or "").strip().lower().startswith(P.AUTO_REVERT + " ") and a.auto_revert_of is None:
        out({"ok": False, "error": f"a --reason starting with \"{P.AUTO_REVERT} \" is reserved for fleet_probation's "
             "auto-revert (--auto-revert-of): reword it"}, 1)
    if a.txn is not None and not P.TXN_RX.fullmatch(a.txn):
        ap.error("--txn must match [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}")
    if a.failure_probe is not None and not P.PROBE_RX.fullmatch(a.failure_probe):
        ap.error("--failure-probe must be a failure probe id fail-<16 hex>")
    if a.probation and a.op == "archive":
        ap.error("--probation applies a rule; an archive is never in probation")
    if a.op == "archive" and (not a.archive_kind or not (a.evidence or "").strip()):
        ap.error("--op archive needs --archive-kind (redundancy|supersession|error) and a non-empty --evidence")
    if a.relation is not None:
        rel = R.parse_relation(a.relation)
        if rel is None or not a.relation.strip():
            ap.error("--relation must be new, refines:<hex id> or supersedes:<hex id>")
        a.relation = rel[0] + (f":{rel[1]}" if rel[1] else "")
    try:
        forced = L.parse_scope_flag(a.scope) if a.scope else None
    except ValueError as e:
        ap.error(str(e))
    if a.revert:
        return revert(a, forced or L.generic_scope())
    if not a.diff or (not a.check and (not a.run or not a.reason)):
        ap.error("DIFF --run RUN --reason TEXT are required (or --revert ID)")
    apply(a, forced)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
